  <conversation ID="Bep">
    <start>
      <choice ID="Vixy_TeachModMicroserrated" Target="Vixy_TaughtModMicroserrated" Ordinal="9700">
        <text>Your teeth are finer than my saw. Show me.</text>
        <part Name="Vixy_TeachMicroserrated" />
      </choice>
    </start>
    <node ID="Vixy_TaughtModMicroserrated">
      <text
      >Serration is teeth. Microserration is teeth on the teeth. Cut smaller, cut smaller, cut smaller - and then the flesh simply agrees to part.</text>
      <choice Target="Start">
        <text>Thank you, =pronouns.formalAddressTerm=.</text>
      </choice>
    </node>
  </conversation>

  <!-- Q Girl teaches massively overloaded. #723.

       One teacher per recipe, so a tinker is a person worth finding rather than one of four
       interchangeable sources. The cost is that killing them removes the recipe from that save.

       Ordinal 9700 puts this below Vixy_ShowMakersMark at 9800 and Vixy_AskName at 10000, and above
       vanilla's water ritual at 980 and [begin trade] at 990 - a thing you ask a tinker about after
       greeting them and before doing business.

       The teaching part carries no fields: which recipe it grants is the subclass, because
       configuration fields on a [Serializable] type become save layout - the same reasoning as the
       eighteen Vixy_Trinket subclasses.

       The choice is invisible unless I already know ModOverloaded, do not know ModMassivelyOverloaded, and hold the
       Tinkering rank its tier requires - Tinker II for all four, one rank above the Tinker I their
       bases sit at. -->
  <conversation ID="Q Girl">
    <start>
      <choice ID="Vixy_TeachModMassivelyOverloaded" Target="Vixy_TaughtModMassivelyOverloaded" Ordinal="9700">
        <text>How far past its rating can a cell actually be pushed?</text>
        <part Name="Vixy_TeachMassivelyOverloaded" />
      </choice>
    </start>
    <node ID="Vixy_TaughtModMassivelyOverloaded">
      <text
      >Further than the plate says. The plate is a promise to a customer, not a limit. Wind the regulator past its stop and hold your breath - it draws far more, and it will tell you when it disagrees.</text>
      <choice Target="Start">
        <text>Thank you, =pronouns.formalAddressTerm=.</text>
      </choice>
    </node>
  </conversation>
</conversations>
